{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787603605504399001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"cibophobic-holohedral-esok","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"95f90fcc9f51de3d50449fd9fb5cd2feb79f84a3d568382143e94a1f91a2d08a","event_uuid":"fb9e1139-4906-493e-93bc-df4e9b4f484c","position":{"commit_sha":"42b7e2363cc437bdc99941cd7303f2405c1e3791","position":"1787594440498360001-fb9e1139-4906-493e-93bc-df4e9b4f484c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"28cdca494d402f5798d76e81079d61db04c46df8ef05ebad33b100fe04148efd","event_uuid":"2cff0724-850a-4133-9d76-951df4aa9017","position":{"commit_sha":"f2c91fd6b3e9a432bb86cf50a41c8d35e45a846a","position":"1787594575142436001-2cff0724-850a-4133-9d76-951df4aa9017"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"50fdb776965fc031818ccbdfea00e732188e9a139c307d406a0564740fd556d2","event_uuid":"9f3dc9a4-8fb1-4343-9567-1688df005064","position":{"commit_sha":"ca0b82f3ed82ba880e6f8ebefceb10b77bdac0e8","position":"1787598290754548001-9f3dc9a4-8fb1-4343-9567-1688df005064"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"3c6589bc27b089680e8223c3d701111dfb628d014593bd9a06323cdd84722707","event_uuid":"3b4cb01a-2ca7-48b1-af25-abbdb6b0e509","position":{"commit_sha":"6652ccbe939358fa1607285e02fde985afb2b9f6","position":"1787600333307568001-3b4cb01a-2ca7-48b1-af25-abbdb6b0e509"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787594440498360001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2cff0724-850a-4133-9d76-951df4aa9017","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"}],"description":"Add the self-contained rebar MCP HTTP service to the box per the ADR (deft-evolutive-mosasaur):\na new `mcp` compose service + `Dockerfile.mcp` running loopback-bound `rebar-mcp` HTTP, and an\nnginx `/mcp/` TLS-edge location with a **switchable upstream** so the autodeploy slice\n(panicky-sylphish-foxterrier) can flip traffic blue→green atomically. INFRA only; the live AWS\nprovision/deploy is approval-gated (a human performs it). Single concern: the on-box MCP service\nand its edge — autodeploy logic lives in foxterrier, secrets in avians.\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`: an `mcp` service (image built from `Dockerfile.mcp`),\n  loopback-published on a new dedicated port, `restart: always`, with a container `healthcheck`\n  hitting the MCP `/health` endpoint. `MCP_PATHS` for the autodeploy change-detector are declared\n  here so foxterrier can consume them.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp`: builds `rebar-mcp` from the same `src/rebar` source the review-bot\n  builds from (shared base layer). Boots with `transport=http`, `http_tls_at_edge=true`, allowed\n  hosts/origins and `auth_resource_server_url` from config, `static` verifier — the ADR-decided\n  fail-closed HTTP posture (ADR 0050 guards: DNS-rebinding/Origin, non-loopback-bind ack).\n- `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`: a new `location /mcp/` proxying to the MCP loopback port via a\n  named `upstream` block whose target is a materialized include (the atomic-flip seam), consistent\n  with the existing `/review/` and header-guarded `/opcert/` patterns. TLS terminates at nginx.\n- A `/health` endpoint on the MCP server exposing an integer `in_flight` gauge that counts ONLY\n  long-running/certified ops (review_plan/verify_completion/review_code/scan_spec), plus a bounded\n  SIGTERM grace window so a retiring container lets an in-flight op finish before exit. The gauge\n  feeds foxterrier's retire check; it does not gate the deploy.\n\n## Approach + rationale\nMirror the proven opcert edge (loopback service + nginx location) but expose a switchable upstream\nrather than a hardcoded `proxy_pass host:port`, because the ADR's blue-green cutover needs to\nre-point the upstream atomically (the local updater's `current`-pointer analog). `/health` counts\nonly expensive ops so retirement waits on billable work, not trivial reads. Shared base image keeps\ndisk/build cost low; the extra retained MCP images are bounded by the existing docker prune.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tier: **real CLI/compose integration** (per test-design §3, \"CLI/streams\" + \"producer/consumer\"):\n  `docker compose up mcp` in a local/staging compose brings the service up healthy; the container\n  `healthcheck` passes against `/health`, and `/health` returns a JSON body with an integer\n  `in_flight` field. Oracle: `in_flight` reads 0 at idle and increments during a simulated\n  long-running op (a stubbed certified tool) and returns to 0 after — asserted via the real\n  endpoint, with a trivial read op NOT moving the gauge (contrast case, §6).\n- [ ] Fail-closed boot: with a non-loopback bind and NO TLS-at-edge/allowlist ack, the server refuses to\n  boot (assert exit non-zero + the ADR-0050 guard message); with the ack + `static` verifier and a\n  valid bearer it serves, and an absent/invalid bearer is rejected 401 through the nginx `/mcp/`\n  edge (oracle: HTTP status from a real request through the rendered nginx config).\n- [ ] The nginx `/mcp/` upstream is a named block sourced from a materialized include (the flip seam\n  foxterrier re-points), verified by `nginx -t` on the rendered template.\n- [ ] SIGTERM grace: sending SIGTERM while a long op is in flight lets it finish within the grace window\n  before the process exits (subprocess/signal test, §7), not an immediate kill.\n\n## Compat / rollback\nPurely additive — new service, new port, new nginx location; touches no existing service. Rollback =\nremove the `mcp` service/location (gerrit/review-bot/opcert unaffected). Security trust-boundary:\nnew authenticated network endpoint — enforced by `static` bearer at the app + TLS at the nginx edge.\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR). Blocks: panicky-sylphish-foxterrier (needs the\nswitchable upstream + `/health`), unmythical-uninspired-olm (needs a reachable endpoint).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"],["parent","jira-reb-3527"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"jira-reb-3527","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fd4a-4e91-f179-4932","ticket_type":"story","title":"rebar-mcp HTTP transport service on the AWS box (compose + Dockerfile + nginx /mcp/ route)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fb9e1139-4906-493e-93bc-df4e9b4f484c","2cff0724-850a-4133-9d76-951df4aa9017","9f3dc9a4-8fb1-4343-9567-1688df005064","3b4cb01a-2ca7-48b1-af25-abbdb6b0e509"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787603605504399001,"uuid":"0c90a2c4-22cc-4133-b8bb-37ab10bce3ab"}